steps.instructions:
The other way to vary a sound is to have several and pick one. The course has two sound files, so the three here are the coin file at three speeds; with more files you would load a different file into each. Three changes, each where a STEP 2 line is. Make all three before you press Run: until the third is done, the miss block still says `thud.play();` when there is no `thud` any more, and the first miss stops the game with a red error that names `thud`.

1. At the top, `let chime, thud;` becomes `let chime, thuds;`.
2. In `setup()`, the two `thud` lines become a list of three sounds, each given its own rate:

```js
thuds = [
  loadSound('/moshion/assets/coin.wav'),
  loadSound('/moshion/assets/coin.wav'),
  loadSound('/moshion/assets/coin.wav'),
];
thuds[0].rate = 0.4;
thuds[1].rate = 0.5;
thuds[2].rate = 0.6;
```

3. In the miss block, `thud.play();` becomes a random pick from the list, the way 5.2.1 picked a random colour:

```js
const pick = floor(random(thuds.length));
thuds[pick].play();
```

`thuds.length` is 3, so `floor(random(3))` is 0, 1 or 2: exactly the three positions. Run it and miss a few on purpose.
